```

## Best Approach

The optimal solution uses the **Euclidean Algorithm** to repeatedly divide the larger dimension by the smaller dimension and count the squares formed.

- **Time Complexity:** `O(log(min(n, m)))`
- **Space Complexity:** `O(1)`

**Note:** Use the optimal solution for submission. All three approaches above use the same greedy idea, so they are not fundamentally different algorithms.
